  "packageSize": 37068947,
  "projectUrl": "https://ssrs2.net/",
  "published": "2026-10-14T18:28:16.447Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.5.0: edit reports from code. ReportEditor (.NET 8, 9 and 10) opens an RDLC or RDL file, outlines it with each item's role (table, totals, declaration, signature...), changes it by short operations (add a text box or a block that collapses when hidden, move or swap items with what is under them following, insert a table row, add a field, copy an item from another report, a Lookup text) or by exact replacements, and saves it as written: what an edit does not touch stays byte for byte, the file's encoding and line ends kept, a file changed since it was read never overwritten. DefinitionStructure groups many reports by their structure and says how they differ. CheckRendering(options) says where each item prints, checks placement rules (order, page, no overlap, page count), renders variants of the data and row counts (the row count from which a page is added) and compares with a baseline definition; it also reports lookups that find no row, conversions that depend on the machine's culture and the fonts text is drawn with (GetFontsUsed, GetItemLayout). Details: https://ssrs2.net",
